WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.650
SPEAKER: In this
video, we're going

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:04.890
to walk through creating a
self-serve online Google Cloud

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.100
billing account.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.240
If you are a Google Cloud
user within an organization,

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.150
you'll need to have the Billing
Account Creator role in order

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.930
to perform this task.

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.890
If you are not a member of
the Google Cloud Organization

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.080
but instead are managing
your Google Cloud

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.800
resources using Projects, you
need no special permissions.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.620
Get started by heading
into the Cloud Console.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.470
You can start on your
Organization or any Project

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.250
homepage.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.430
Then head to the Navigation
menu in the left-hand pane,

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:36.570
choose Billing, and then
click Manage Billing Accounts.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.730
If you land in the
Billing Overview page,

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.580
like we did here, you can
navigate to Manage Billing

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.380
Accounts by expanding
the dropdown

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.450
list of Billing Accounts.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.460
Click Create Account.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.630
Give your account a name.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.480
Choose your
Organization, if this

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.000
is applicable in
your case, and select

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.910
the country that corresponds
to your billing address.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.240
This will determine your
payment options and currency.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.880
Note, you cannot change the
country for a billing account

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.440
after it is created.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.180
Click Continue.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:09.090
Next, select an existing
Payments profile,

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.690
or create a new one.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:15.170
A Payments profile stores your
payment instrument information

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:18.380
and defines how you pay for
charges across all of Google.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.520
To use an existing
Payments profile,

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.940
you must have sign-up
and purchase or Admin

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:26.030
with all permissions for
the Payments profile.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:28.160
Note that permissions
for the Payments profile

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:31.490
are set by visiting
pay.google.com and not using

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.130
the Google Cloud IAM service.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.450
If creating a new
Payments profile,

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.720
you must indicate
your account type.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.080
Select Business if this is
for a business, organization,

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.850
partnership, or
educational institution.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.910
Otherwise, select Individual.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:50.810
Note, the account type cannot be
changed after profile creation.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.090
Then choose a payment method.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.280
Check the documentation
for more information

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.850
on which payment methods are
available for your country.

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:02.450
Finally, enter your
payment method details.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:05.030
Click Submit and Enable Billing.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.790
Congratulations, you
can now link projects

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.600
to this billing account.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.560
Note that by default, the person
who creates the Cloud Billing

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.780
account is a billing
account administrator

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.700
for the Cloud Billing account.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.070
To learn more about
updating billing account

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:22.070
and Payments profile
settings after creation,

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.750
follow the link in
the description,

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:25.700
or head over to
the documentation

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.410
to check out more details.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.460
[MUSIC PLAYING]

